{"id":"346a8eb2725975f8","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-thm-coding-universe.md","title":"Continuum-Sized Almost Disjoint Family","display":"thm-coding-universe — Continuum-Sized Almost Disjoint Family","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-coding-universe","aliases":["58-thm-coding-universe","Coding the Universe","Almost Disjoint Coding"],"display":"thm-coding-universe — Continuum-Sized Almost Disjoint Family","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-powerset.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-coding-universe"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-coding-universe</span><span>Coding the Universe</span><span>Almost Disjoint Coding</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-coding-universe — Continuum-Sized Almost Disjoint Family"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" href=\"?note=2b6b1d9eb78a2714\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-powerset.md\">../batch09/58-df-powerset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-finite.md\">../batch04/58-df-finite.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2^{&lt;\\omega}\">\\(2^{&lt;\\omega}\\)</span> is the countable binary tree and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"b:\\omega\\to2^{&lt;\\omega}\">\\(b:\\omega\\to2^{&lt;\\omega}\\)</span> is a bijection.</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\\in2^\\omega\">\\(x\\in2^\\omega\\)</span>, let <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_x=\\{b^{-1}(x\\upharpoonright n):n\\in\\omega\\}\">\\(A_x=\\{b^{-1}(x\\upharpoonright n):n\\in\\omega\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-finite.md\">../batch04/58-df-finite.md</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}coding\\text{-}universe}\\vdash\n\\mathcal A\\coloneqq\\{A_x:x\\in2^\\omega\\}\n\\to\n\\left[\n\\mathcal A\\subseteq[\\omega]^\\omega\n\\land|\\mathcal A|=2^{\\aleph_0}\n\\land\\forall A\\neq B\\in\\mathcal A\\;\n\\mathrm{Finite}(A\\cap B)\n\\right].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}coding\\text{-}universe}\\vdash\n\\mathcal A\\coloneqq\\{A_x:x\\in2^\\omega\\}\n\\to\n\\left[\n\\mathcal A\\subseteq[\\omega]^\\omega\n\\land|\\mathcal A|=2^{\\aleph_0}\n\\land\\forall A\\neq B\\in\\mathcal A\\;\n\\mathrm{Finite}(A\\cap B)\n\\right].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Distinct branches share only their common initial segments, so the family is almost disjoint.</li>\n<li>This theorem supplies a combinatorial coding substrate; it does not by itself code the entire universe. Stronger Jensen coding statements require additional hypotheses and separate definitions.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-powerset.md","status":"resolved","id":"2b6b1d9eb78a2714","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-powerset.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-finite.md","status":"resolved","id":"d9a25b0ac94a3598","ancho